{"id":1,"explanation":"The nonce check in verify rejects a token whose nonce has already been seen. Removing it would let an old token be used again. #123 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":2,"explanation":"Call ensure_key_salt before creating KeyManager. If salt setup fails, startup must stop instead of initializing the manager.","unsure":""}
{"id":3,"explanation":"Before allocating buf with topN elements, keep topN at or below maxSimpleTopN so the slice stays at or below 1 MiB. maxSimpleTopN is the named limit.","unsure":""}
{"id":4,"explanation":"When meta.abi_version is absent, the mapping must produce None. Treating absence as the current ABI would incorrectly accept missing version information. #1784 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":5,"explanation":"The drop-in written under /etc/tlp.d/ can be overridden by /etc/tlp.conf because TLP reads that file last. Both paths are TLP configuration locations.","unsure":""}
{"id":6,"explanation":"The set_key call relies on TLP version 1.10 or later. _AC, _BAT and _SAV name profile suffixes; the key being set uses _BAT. Leaving the corresponding _AC setting unset preserves GNOME's Performance toggle.","unsure":""}
{"id":7,"explanation":"For a JsonException, this catch block returns null. The caller then logs the warning, so this block deliberately does not log or propagate the parse error.","unsure":""}
{"id":8,"explanation":"When AllowedTools is set, RemoveSkipPermissions must remove --dangerously-skip-permissions from args. That flag bypasses the restrictions supplied through --allowedTools.","unsure":""}
{"id":9,"explanation":"For the dead-code decision in thunk_is_dead, consult is_definitely_dead_code in rust/xray-core/src/compiler/graph_preamble.rs. The comment points to a verdict table there.","unsure":"The comment does not say which verdict in the table applies to this function."}
{"id":10,"explanation":"Replace the fixed repos_skipped value with one derived from the domains-to-repos mapping. #874 tracks that work.","unsure":""}
{"id":11,"explanation":"index.regex_query(pattern) uses a linear-time DFA, so the regex search does not incur backtracking.","unsure":""}
{"id":12,"explanation":"The refresh_tokens schema is coupled to RefreshTokenSqliteBackend._ensure_schema in src/storage/refresh_token_backend.py. Changes to the token-family tables must be coordinated with that method.","unsure":""}
{"id":13,"explanation":"MAX_BATCH is 500 because the vendor's batch API accepts at most 500 items per request. doc:vendor-api#limits points to the limits section of the vendor API documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":14,"explanation":"The numeric Status values must stay aligned with STATUS_LABELS in web/src/status.ts. Reordering these iota declarations would assign different meanings to integers already stored. #88 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":15,"explanation":"Keep tenant_id first and created_at second in this index. That order matches the orders_by_tenant query; orders_by_tenant names the query that depends on it.","unsure":""}
{"id":16,"explanation":"TList.Add must preserve the rule that FCount never exceeds Length(FItems). Grow is the operation that maintains enough capacity.","unsure":""}
{"id":17,"explanation":"In close, flush buffered data before closing the sink. Closing drops _buf, so reversing the calls could lose data.","unsure":""}
{"id":18,"explanation":"userPath comes from a request. Resolve it relative to workspaceRoot and reject paths that escape that root through .. components; normalization alone does not show the required rejection.","unsure":""}
{"id":19,"explanation":"Drain the ring before freeing buf. Otherwise the IRQ handler can access freed memory while processing the ring. #2201 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":20,"explanation":"items.reserve(n) is intended to make one allocation before insertion. Repeated growth during push_back accounted for 40% of the measured profile. doc:perf-notes#ingest points to the ingest section of the performance notes.","unsure":""}
{"id":21,"explanation":"Keep HOLDLOCK on this SQL Server MERGE so concurrent upserts do not race. doc:mssql-merge#concurrency points to the concurrency guidance for MERGE.","unsure":""}
{"id":22,"explanation":"PRAGMA AUTONOMOUS_TRANSACTION makes the audit write independent of the caller's transaction, allowing the audit row to survive a caller rollback.","unsure":""}
{"id":23,"explanation":"This migration creates a replacement table because SQLite ALTER TABLE cannot drop the needed constraints directly. doc:sqlite-alter#otheralter points to the relevant ALTER TABLE documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":24,"explanation":"The loop scans every five seconds because NFS mounts do not emit the inotify events this code would need for change notifications.","unsure":""}
{"id":25,"explanation":"Keep the awaited run(job) calls in a for...of loop. Using await inside forEach would let errors escape the intended try/catch.","unsure":""}
{"id":26,"explanation":"The Vec<u8> returned by read_frame must have a length no greater than MAX_FRAME. The decoder enforces that by rejecting larger frames.","unsure":""}
{"id":27,"explanation":"Register drainHook before pool.start() so the pool has its SIGTERM cleanup hook as soon as it starts. The hook drains the pool during shutdown.","unsure":""}
{"id":28,"explanation":"Move the hard-coded two-second retry policy into configuration. The work is done when Default in internal/retry/policy.go reads that configuration; #Default names the symbol in that file.","unsure":""}
{"id":29,"explanation":"Issue #412 contains the full matrix of allowed transitions among LeaseState values, including Active, Released and Stale.","unsure":""}
{"id":30,"explanation":"Pass TOKEN to tool login through standard input only. Putting it in argv would expose it through ps to other users.","unsure":""}
{"id":31,"explanation":"Create app_reader before granting it SELECT privileges. Migration 042 expects that role to exist.","unsure":""}
{"id":32,"explanation":"Make on_event safe to run more than once for the same webhook because Stripe may retry delivery for three days. doc:stripe#webhook-retries points to the webhook retry documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":33,"explanation":"Compare sig and expected with hmac.Equal. Its constant-time comparison avoids the timing leak that a == comparison could create for MACs.","unsure":""}
{"id":34,"explanation":"Build CodeGraph once per index, at a cost proportional to the number of edges. Do not rebuild it for each query.","unsure":""}
{"id":35,"explanation":"Changing TCustomerRec's packed layout would make existing saved .dat files incompatible. Bump FILE_VERSION if the layout changes.","unsure":""}
{"id":36,"explanation":"Keep MSG_MAX and MSG_MAX_WIRE in proto/messages.h synchronized. Changing this 4096-byte limit requires changing the corresponding wire limit.","unsure":""}
{"id":37,"explanation":"handler assumes authMiddleware has run and established a non-null session.userId. Code or types around the handler must preserve that condition.","unsure":""}
{"id":38,"explanation":"The cache check and subsequent put must happen atomically. Synchronizing on cache protects that whole sequence; using ConcurrentHashMap alone would not make separate check and put operations atomic.","unsure":""}
{"id":39,"explanation":"raw is a user-provided repository alias. validate_alias must check it against the registry before it is used in a path join, preventing an untrusted alias from selecting an unintended path. #1996 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":40,"explanation":"Rows inserted into Payments must have a nonnegative Amount. Refunds are represented as separate rows with Kind = 'R', rather than negative Amount values.","unsure":""}
{"id":41,"explanation":"Set stop_ before joining worker_. Otherwise the worker may keep running and join() can block forever.","unsure":""}
{"id":42,"explanation":"The limiter accounts for GitHub's stated limit of 5,000 API requests per hour per token. doc:github-rest#rate-limits points to the REST API rate-limit documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":43,"explanation":"Stop the cidx service before installing its replacement binary at /usr/local/bin/cidx. Replacing the running binary could fail with “Text file busy.”","unsure":""}
{"id":44,"explanation":"Do not share the _lease CredentialLease across jobs. Sharing it could expose one user's credentials to another user's job. #77 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":45,"explanation":"Keep len(ids) at or below 999 before binding ids into this DELETE statement. The comment identifies 999 as the SQLite bound-variable limit for one statement.","unsure":""}
{"id":46,"explanation":"If cgroup.create(limit) fails, warn and continue the job. A bad memory estimate should degrade containment rather than abort the job.","unsure":""}
{"id":47,"explanation":"Remove the legacy /v1/jobs route. #530 tracks that work; /v1 is the legacy route prefix.","unsure":""}
{"id":48,"explanation":"The session model in doc:adr-007#session-model explains why SessionRegistry keeps sessions per tab. The reference points to the session-model section of ADR 007.","unsure":""}
{"id":49,"explanation":"This partial index covers only lease rows where released_at IS NULL, matching active-lease lookups by credential_id. The comment reports a 30-fold speedup for that lookup.","unsure":""}
{"id":50,"explanation":"Keep the EVENT_TYPES values synchronized with EVENT_LABELS in web/src/events.ts and the event documentation in docs/events.md. Both paths identify places to update when event types change.","unsure":""}
